  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Bishop Conference</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD South Sudan Programme together with other CI member agencies continue to work closely with the Bishop Conference Secretariat in Juba aimed at:
a) Enhancing the role of the Catholic Church towards effective delivery of humanitarian aid
b) Participation of the church in major national agenda geared towards promoting Catholic Values within the society
c) Through indirect assistance in the peace process by mobilizing and supporting the Bishops&apos; strong engagement in the reconciliation process by espousing the spirit of brotherhood.
CAFOD SS contributes to the above key areas through the following mechanisms:
a) Jointly with other CI members in Juba discuss the Bishops&apos; meeting agenda and pledge financial support towards such meetings.
b) Assist directly or through reimbursement of costs incurred - the logistical/movement of the Bishops from different locations in South Sudan including Sudan to a central meeting at place at the Secretariat office in Juba.

In the current financial year, the Secretariat have shared detailed plans of 2 plenary meetings to be held in Juba. CAFOD SS is therefore committed to continue with its annual engagement with the Bishops&apos; plenary meetings and any other meetings that maybe convened in the current year. CAFOD has made financial commitment based on agreed budgets and shall contribute to the Secretariat based upon actual invoices presented to CAFOD.</narrative>
  </description>
